# React Components

Map of this area: `docs/architecture/ui.md`; store hooks and selectors: `docs/architecture/app.md`.

## Files
- One component per file; file name equals component name (`ToolToggle.tsx`).
- A subcomponent used by a single parent lives in the parent folder (`Board/Cell.tsx`).
- No barrel `index.ts` files.

## Logic out of components
- Non-trivial logic (derived state, handlers with rules, effects) goes in a `useXxx.ts` hook next to
  the component. Components stay presentational.

```tsx
// BAD: rules inside the component body
const axis = Math.abs(dx) > Math.abs(dy) ? 'row' : 'col'
// GOOD
const { bind, strokeCount } = usePaintStroke()
```

## Size
- Keep components under ~150 lines. Split when they grow.

## Props and state
- Type props as `XxxProps` above the component.
- No prop drilling deeper than 2 levels: use a store selector instead.
- Use granular Zustand selectors, never the whole store. Wrap hot list items (cells) in `memo`.

## Accessibility
- Semantic elements (`button`, never clickable `div`), `aria-label` from strings, visible focus.
